## Example: Full Mockup-First Flow

**User request:** "Build the application review page for admins"

**Agent response:**

> This task involves building a new admin page with table/card layout and approval actions. Would you like to:
> A) **Mockup-first** — See a working prototype with sample applications, refine layout/interactions, then build backend
> B) **Full-stack** — Build controller + service + page together (standard workflow)

**User:** "A, mockup first"

**Agent:**

```
MOCKUP PLANNING for BD-042: Admin application review page

UI CONTRACTS:
- Route: /admin/applications/review
- Layout: AdminLayout (sidebar + header)
- Data shape: Application { id, applicant_name, status, submitted_at, documents[] }

MOCKUP SCOPE:
- Components: ApplicationCard, ApprovalButton, StatusBadge
- Interactions: Approve button (simulated), status filter dropdown
- States: Empty (no applications), loading (simulated), populated (5 sample apps)
- Mock data: 5 realistic applications with varied statuses

VISUAL QUESTIONS:
- Should this match existing Admin/Users/Index.svelte table style?
- Prefer cards or table layout?
- Mobile-responsive needed for Phase 1?

Confirm mockup scope? (Y/n)
```

**User:** "Yes, use cards like the users page, desktop-only for now"

**Agent builds mockup, runs dev server, takes screenshot:**

```
MOCKUP READY: http://localhost/admin/applications/review

[Screenshot attached]

IMPLEMENTED:
- ApplicationCard: Shows applicant name, status badge, submission date
- ApprovalButton: Click logs to console, simulates 500ms backend call
- StatusFilter: Dropdown filters by pending/approved/rejected
- Mock data: 5 sample applications
- States: Empty state card, loading spinner on approve

INTERACTIVE ELEMENTS:
- Approve button: Simulates approval, updates status badge
- Filter dropdown: Filters cards by status

Please review and provide feedback:
- Layout/spacing OK?
- Missing any UI elements?
- Any state/interaction issues?
- Ready to proceed with backend integration?
```

**User:** "Add a 'View Details' button to each card"

**Agent updates mockup, shows new screenshot:**

```
Updated mockup with "View Details" button (currently logs application ID to console).

[New screenshot]

Any other changes, or ready to build backend?
```

**User:** "Looks good, build it"

**Agent:**

```
Mockup approved. Building real implementation:

BACKEND WORK:
- Controller: Admin/ApplicationController@review
- Service: ApplicationReviewService (approval logic)
- Form Request: ApproveApplicationRequest (validation)
- Policy: ApplicationPolicy@approve (admin-only check)

FRONTEND WORK:
- Replace mock data with Inertia props from controller
- Wire up Approve button to POST /admin/applications/{id}/approve
- Add error handling (validation errors, unauthorized)
- Add Inertia progress indicator for loading state

TESTS:
- test_admin_can_view_review_page
- test_admin_can_approve_application
- test_non_admin_cannot_approve
- test_approve_with_invalid_id_returns_404

Proceed with full build? (Y/n)
```

**User:** "Yes"

**Agent follows standard TDD workflow, builds backend + integrates frontend, runs tests, commits.**

