## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

| Anti-Pattern | Problem | Fix |
|--------------|---------|-----|
| Mockup without user confirmation | Builds wrong UI, wasted work | Always show screenshot and get approval before backend |
| Placeholder mockups | "TODO: Add table here" defeats purpose | Build fully functional mockup with realistic data |
| Backend calls in mockup | Couples mockup to backend, defeats isolation | Use inline mock data and setTimeout for async simulation |
| Skipping edge cases | Mockup only shows happy path | Include empty state, loading, error states in mockup |
| No screenshot | User can't review without running locally | Always provide screenshot in first presentation |

---

## Success Metrics

**Mockup-first is working when:**

- User says "perfect, build it" after 1-2 refinements
- No UI rework needed after backend integration
- Mockup accurately predicted data structure needs
- User catches layout issues before backend work starts

**Mockup-first is NOT working when:**

- User requests major changes after backend is built
- Mockup doesn't match data model (requires refactor)
- Mockup takes longer than full-stack would have
- User says "just build it" repeatedly (wrong use case)

---

## Quick Decision Tree

```
Is this a frontend task?
├─ No → Use standard agentic workflow
└─ Yes → Is it visually complex or new UI pattern?
    ├─ No (simple form, existing pattern) → Use standard workflow
    └─ Yes → Offer mockup-first option
        ├─ User accepts → Follow Mockup-Builder-Agent workflow
        └─ User declines → Use standard workflow
```

---

## Summary

Mockup-Builder-Agent is **not a replacement** for agentic workflow. It's an **optional execution mode** for frontend work that benefits from visual confirmation.

**Use it when:**
- Building new pages or complex UI flows
- User wants to see before committing to implementation
- Visual design is uncertain or needs iteration

**Skip it when:**
- Building simple forms or CRUD pages with established patterns
- Backend-first makes more sense (API design is the blocker)
- User explicitly requests full-stack approach

**Integration:** Triggered during Session Start Ritual (Step 4) or Implementation Phase (Step 7: UI work). Maintains beads, phase alignment, and inquiry-first principles throughout.
